    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Solomon Islands prime minister Matthew Wale has signed a treaty with Australian prime minister Anthony Albanese naming Australia the \"primary security partner\".",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-25:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The treaty follows the ending of the 2022 security pact with China and the Solomon Islands' decision not to renew it.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-25:12",
        "wiki:rev:1387926936:24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Foreign relations exist between Australia and Solomon Islands, and the two leaders signed the new security pact on 25 November 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1387926936:0",
        "wiki:rev:1387926936:24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-25T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On the map, Solomon Islands is where the reports place it.",
